CAT = "cpaaudAuditReports"; SEG = "ARP"
Q = [
("In an auditor's report on a nonissuer under AU-C 700, which section comes first?",
 "Opinion", ["Basis for Opinion", "Responsibilities of Management", "Key Audit Matters"],
 "Since SAS 134, the Opinion section comes first, followed directly by the Basis for Opinion section."),
("The Basis for Opinion section of an unmodified report for a nonissuer states that the auditor is:",
 "Independent of the entity", ["Liable for any fraud found", "Paid a fixed fee in advance", "Registered with the SEC"],
 "It states that the audit followed GAAS, that the auditor is independent and has met other ethical responsibilities, and that the evidence is sufficient and appropriate."),
("The auditor's report should be dated no earlier than the date on which the auditor has:",
 "Sufficient appropriate evidence", ["Sent the final invoice", "Signed the engagement letter", "Released the report to the client"],
 "Evidence includes that all the statements, including disclosures, were prepared and management has asserted responsibility for them."),
("Statements contain a material misstatement that is not pervasive. The auditor issues:",
 "A qualified opinion", ["An adverse opinion", "A disclaimer of opinion", "An unmodified opinion"],
 "A material but not pervasive misstatement leads to a qualified opinion. If the misstatement were pervasive, the opinion would be adverse."),
("Statements are materially and pervasively misstated because consolidation was not done. The auditor issues:",
 "An adverse opinion", ["A qualified opinion", "A disclaimer of opinion", "An unmodified opinion"],
 "When misstatements are both material and pervasive, the auditor expresses an adverse opinion that the statements are not fairly presented."),
("The auditor cannot obtain sufficient appropriate evidence, and the possible effects are material and pervasive. The auditor issues:",
 "A disclaimer of opinion", ["An adverse opinion", "A qualified opinion", "An unmodified opinion"],
 "An inability to obtain evidence whose possible effects are material and pervasive leads to a disclaimer. If material but not pervasive, the opinion is qualified."),
("An emphasis-of-matter paragraph in a nonissuer report refers to a matter that is:",
 "Appropriately presented or disclosed", ["Materially misstated in the statements", "Not yet audited by the auditor", "Outside the statements entirely"],
 "It draws attention to a matter properly presented or disclosed that is fundamental to users' understanding, such as a major catastrophe. It does not modify the opinion."),
("An other-matter paragraph in an auditor's report refers to a matter that is:",
 "Not presented in the statements", ["A material misstatement found", "A lawsuit disclosed in the notes", "A change in accounting principle"],
 "It covers matters other than those presented or disclosed that are relevant to users' understanding of the audit, the auditor's responsibilities or the report."),
("A nonissuer changes its inventory method from FIFO to weighted average, accounts for it properly, and discloses it. The auditor's report includes:",
 "An emphasis-of-matter paragraph", ["A qualified opinion for the change", "An other-matter paragraph", "No reference to the change"],
 "A justified change in accounting principle with a material effect is highlighted in an emphasis-of-matter paragraph, and the opinion is unmodified."),
("Under PCAOB AS 3101, a critical audit matter is one communicated to the audit committee that relates to material accounts or disclosures and:",
 "Involved especially challenging judgment", ["Was first found by internal audit", "Was corrected by management before issue", "Involved a related party transaction"],
 "A CAM arises from the audit, was communicated or required to be communicated to the audit committee, relates to material accounts or disclosures and involved especially challenging, subjective or complex auditor judgment."),
("Which item must the auditor's report on an issuer's statements include under AS 3101?",
 "The year the auditor began serving", ["The total fee for the audit", "The engagement partner's home state", "The number of staff on the audit"],
 "AS 3101 requires a statement of the year the auditor began serving consecutively as the company's auditor."),
("For an issuer audit, the auditor reports critical audit matters for most companies, but not for:",
 "Emerging growth companies", ["Large accelerated filers", "Banks and savings institutions", "Foreign private issuers"],
 "CAM requirements do not apply to audits of emerging growth companies, brokers and dealers, investment companies other than business development companies, and employee benefit plans."),
("In an integrated audit of an issuer, the auditor finds a material weakness. The opinion on internal control over financial reporting is:",
 "Adverse", ["Qualified", "A disclaimer", "Unmodified with emphasis"],
 "Under AS 2201, one or more material weaknesses require an adverse opinion on ICFR. The opinion on the statements may still be unmodified."),
("In an integrated audit, the reports on the statements and on internal control should be dated:",
 "The same date", ["One month apart", "At the year-end date", "When management signs"],
 "AS 2201 requires the two reports to carry the same date, whether they are combined or issued separately."),
("AS 2201 directs the auditor of internal control to start with the financial statements, entity-level controls and significant accounts. This is the:",
 "Top-down approach", ["Bottom-up approach", "Substantive approach", "Cycle approach"],
 "The top-down approach starts at the statement level and works down to significant accounts, relevant assertions and the controls that address them."),
("A predecessor auditor reissues its report on prior-year statements shown for comparison. The predecessor should first:",
 "Read the current statements", ["Repeat the full audit", "Ask the successor to sign", "Date it at the new date only"],
 "Before reissuing, the predecessor reads the current statements, compares them with the prior ones and obtains representation letters from management and the successor."),
]
